<translate>
<!--T:1-->
{{SITENAME}} runs in three ways. On Linux the standalone binary is the simplest, a single file with no Docker. On macOS or Windows, use the Docker image. Build from source if you want to modify {{SITENAME}} or run an unreleased version.

<!--T:2-->
<span id="binary"></span>
== Binary ==

<!--T:3-->
A single self-contained executable that embeds MediaWiki, for Linux on x86_64 and arm64. Download it and make it executable:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
curl -L -o wikven https://github.com/chaotic-ground/wikven/releases/latest/download/wikven-linux-x86_64
chmod +x wikven
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:4-->
On arm64, use <code>wikven-linux-aarch64</code>. See [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Standalone binary</tvar>|Standalone binary]] for installing it onto your <code>PATH</code>, nightly builds, and the optional host tools it uses.
</translate>

<span id="Docker"></span>
== Docker ==

<translate>
<!--T:6-->
Works on any platform with [https://www.docker.com/ Docker], so it is the option to use on macOS and Windows. The image is published to the GitHub Container Registry:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
docker pull ghcr.io/chaotic-ground/wikven
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:12-->
The same image is published to Quay as well, at <code>quay.io/chaotic-ground/wikven</code>. One build pushes both addresses, so pull from whichever one answers.

<!--T:7-->
The untagged image is the newest released version. To hold a build still, pin the version tag <code>:<tvar name="1">{{WIKVENVERSION}}</tvar></code> or the digest (<code>ghcr.io/chaotic-ground/wikven@sha256:...</code>); shorter tags for the major and the minor version are published too, and move as that line gains releases. A dated <code>nightly-YYYY-MM-DD</code> tag is the main branch as it stood that day, for trying a change before it is released.

<!--T:8-->
<span id="build-from-source"></span>
== Build from source ==

<!--T:9-->
To modify {{SITENAME}} or run an unreleased commit, clone the repository and build the image yourself:
</translate>

<syntaxhighlight lang="shell" copy>
git clone https://github.com/chaotic-ground/wikven.git
cd wikven
docker build -t wikven .
</syntaxhighlight>

<translate>
<!--T:10-->
This produces a local <code>wikven</code> image you run exactly like the published one. To build the standalone binary from source instead, see [https://github.com/chaotic-ground/wikven/blob/main/binary.Dockerfile <code>binary.Dockerfile</code>].

<!--T:13-->
== Which MediaWiki ==

<!--T:14-->
You do not install MediaWiki: every way of running {{SITENAME}} brings its own. The image and the binary are built on '''MediaWiki 1.46''', and that is what renders your pages however you run them.

<!--T:15-->
{{SITENAME}} itself requires MediaWiki 1.46 or later, and every change to it is tested against both 1.46 and MediaWiki's development branch. That is the range it is known to work in, and it is what to build against if you are building from source onto a MediaWiki of your own.
</translate>

----

<translate>
<!--T:11-->
Once you have {{SITENAME}}, head to [[<tvar name="1">Special:MyLanguage/Getting Started</tvar>|Getting Started]] to build your first site.
</translate>

